{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_overview_http_module", "label": "HTTP module (extension, not a BrokerActor)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "HTTP servers do not fit the one-connection-many-messages shape of the I/O broker actors, so they get their own DSL and backend abstraction."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_overview_route_dsl", "label": "Route DSL (path / get / post / concat)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Builds an in-memory route tree that bind() flattens and registers with the chosen backend."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_overview_httpserverbackend", "label": "HttpServerBackend interface", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "All three backends implement it so the route DSL compiles identically; the backend only owns the listen/dispatch loop."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_overview_fastifybackend", "label": "FastifyBackend (default)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_overview_expressbackend", "label": "ExpressBackend (peer dependency)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_overview_honobackend", "label": "HonoBackend (peer dependency)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_overview_httpclient", "label": "Shared HttpClient (singleRequest)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Wraps the runtime native fetch, so it works identically on Bun, Node and Deno."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_overview_client_bounds", "label": "Bounds every client call carries", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A response is buffered before the caller sees it, so the three things the peer controls are bounded by default: 30 s deadline, 8 MiB body, 5 redirect hops. Every bound is enforced by a comparison and a NaN loses one silently \u2014 a NaN timeout arms no timer, an Infinity ceiling never trips \u2014 so an out-of-domain value throws OptionsError before a socket opens."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_overview_httpresponsetoolargeerror", "label": "HttpResponseTooLargeError", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The request is aborted while the body is still arriving, so an oversized or endless response never finishes allocating."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_overview_redirect_policy", "label": "Redirect policy (follow / error / manual)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The client follows redirects itself so decisions happen between hops: a cross-origin hop loses authorization, cookie and proxy-authorization; a 303 (and a 301/302 after POST) continues as GET with the body dropped; non-http(s) targets are refused; deadline and byte ceiling are cumulative. Refusals happen before the hop is issued, because a check on where a chain ended up has already made every request in it."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_overview_httpclientoptions", "label": "HttpClientOptions / newClient", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Give a whole integration its own client instead of loosening the one every actor shares; precedence is request > client > HOCON (actor-ts.http.client) > built-in defaults, and a bare new HttpClient() with no system keeps the built-in numbers."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_overview_middleware_set", "label": "Middleware set (cache / rate limit / idempotency)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each is a handler wrapper composed by nesting at the handler level."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_overview_cache_isolation", "label": "Give each middleware its own cache", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "InMemoryCache is LRU-bounded at 10 000 entries and evicts entries carrying no guarantee first, but it does not rank guarantees against each other \u2014 so varying the Idempotency-Key still evicts rate-limit counters and idempotency records once nothing cheaper is left."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_overview_handler_as_adapter", "label": "HTTP handler as a thin adapter to actors", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Parse the request, ask an actor, marshal the reply. Route handlers run concurrently, so plain mutable state outside actors races; and a slow handler occupies a connection lifetime, so heavy work belongs behind an ask with a sane timeout."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_overview_http_module", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_overview_route_dsl", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_overview_http_module", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_overview_httpserverbackend", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_overview_httpserverbackend", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_overview_fastifybackend", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_overview_httpserverbackend", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_overview_expressbackend", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_overview_httpserverbackend", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_overview_honobackend", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight"